        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Example 1 as shown in Figure H.5 shows an example certificate structure. In this example, the SECC certificate originates from the V2G root CA certificate chain. All other main actors like the eMSP and the OEM utilize their own root certificates for the leaf certificates like the contract certificate, vehicle certificate, etc. In this example, none of the certificates are cross signed. This means that the SECC needs the OEM root CA certificate to validate the vehicle certificate during TLS session setup.",
